Print the coalescing equation when a chunk cannot be grown

The HWM retry did not change the outcome: there is no "chunk high watermark
keeps moving" panic, so that branch now passes and the NULL comes from the
adjacent-free-run check.  q is the size class request, n is what is left after
merging, f is the real length of the adjacent free run and m its marker.  The
check requires f == q - n; printing all four turns the guess into a reading.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c b/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
--- a/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
+++ b/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
@@ -3024,7 +3024,10 @@
 		if (adj_free_meta) {
 			if (adj_free_meta->km_page_marker != KMEM_META_FREE ||
 			    kmem_get_free_chunk_len(adj_free_meta) !=
 			    meta_req - meta_num) {
+				printf("\nA q=%u n=%u f=%u m=%x\n", meta_req, meta_num,
+				    kmem_get_free_chunk_len(adj_free_meta),
+				    adj_free_meta->km_page_marker);
 				return NULL;
 			}
 		}
